{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"00b319d7ae838cc3d3bba24368ea64c217cac19ea4aca8fe59d45eca2dc63c2f","digest":{"component_or_area":"ticket close command","key_entities":["src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py","src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py","_compact_on_close","_compact_locked",".ticket-write.lock.d","compact_txn._git","gitutil.run_git_write","tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_compact_on_close_skip_7084.py","tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_does_not_compact_barbet.py","docs/concurrency.md"],"problem_keywords":["lock contention","write lock hold","compaction","performance","ticket close","blocking"],"propositions":["Closing a ticket invokes _compact_on_close which acquires and holds the store write lock for unbounded duration (measured 13m53s) while performing fold, snapshot write, and git operations, blocking concurrent agent writes","The store write lock hold during compaction stacks nested advisory flocks and timeout budgets that are acquired but never released until the entire compaction completes, causing agents to exhaust acquisition budgets and lose writes","Compaction is optional housekeeping not required for correctness; the event log remains valid and the reducer replays unfolded events correctly","Removing _compact_on_close from the close path restores lock-hold duration to seconds while preserving correctness and deferring compaction to explicit out-of-band invocation via rebar compact command"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787411687333364001,"uuid":"2be25980-430b-4fc1-b18c-d0d5bbc1b7bc"}